      "name": "Mrs. Sato",
      "role": "elderly farmer",
      "persona": "Eighty and stubborn, she has worked these terraces since she was a girl and trusts weather over people. She wants the bell rung again but will not say who silenced it.",
      "knowledge": [
        "The bell stopped the night of the autumn festival, after the lanterns went out.",
        "Someone from the valley cannot carry the message; the ridge keeps what it is told by locals.",
        "The old path to the ridge starts behind the Old Rice Barn, past the persimmon racks."
      ],
      "secrets": [
        "Her son went up the ridge the night of the festival and has not come down."
